  Wizards are restricted in Bow.  For multishot missile weapons Expert
skill is critical. 

  The following roles can get to Expert with at least one multishot
missile weapon.  If no starting skill is mentioned then they start
unskilled.


  Healers: Darts only.  2x average damage at Expert.

  Rangers: Expert in all multishot ranged weapons.  They also get a 
role bonus chance of an additional missile with such.  2.5x average
damage at Expert.  ('Range'rs.  Get it?)  They start with 80-100 arrows
and basic skill in bow.  They'll get the Longbow of Diana.  Elven/orcish
rangers using racial bow/arrows get a racial bonus arrow chance, average
3x arrows.  Elves get +1 dmg per elven arrow fired from Elven Bow.
Expert in divination spells to use as fire-control radar for missiles.
(Skilled+ spell of Detect Monsters.)


  Rogues: Daggers 2.5x, darts 2x, crossbow 2x.  Role bonus dagger
possibility for daggers only.  Start with 6-15 racial daggers and basic
skill in daggers.  2.5x damage throwing expert daggers.  (Backstab bonus
on fleeing monsters when not #twoweaponing.)

    Samurai: Shuriken 2x and bow 2x.  Start with bow and 26 to 45 ya
(bamboo arrows) and basic skill in bow.  2.5x when firing Expert ya from
a yumi.  +1 dmg per ya when fired from yumi.

 Tourist: Daggers, 2x damage, Darts, 2x damage.  Start with 21 to 40 +2
darts and basic skill in darts.  (Note ability to blessed charge rings
of increase damage with PYEC.  2x the damage bonus.)

  Valkyrie: Daggers only, 2x.  Start with a single +0 dagger and basic
skill in dagger.

  Wizards: Daggers or darts, 2x damage.  Magicbane (guaranteed first
divine gift) uses dagger skill.



Other:
  Knights can get to skilled with the crossbow: 1.5x damage.
  Cavemen can get to skilled with the bow: 1.5x damage.




